minimum_number_of_taps_to_open_to_water_.brute:
for each size from 0 to n + 1:
    for each subset of taps of that size:
        wet = array of n false values, one per unit segment
        for each tap i in the subset:
            mark segments max(0, i - ranges[i]) .. min(n, i + ranges[i]) - 1 as wet
        if every segment is wet: return size   (smallest size first: the first hit wins)
return -1

candy.brute:
candies = array of n ones
changed = true
while changed:
    changed = false
    for each child i:
        for each neighbour j of i (left and right):
            if j is in bounds and ratings[i] > ratings[j] and candies[i] <= candies[j]:
                candies[i] = candies[j] + 1   (one step of the fix; the rest ripples in later sweeps)
                changed = true
return sum of candies

candy.optimal:
candies = array of n ones
for each i from 1 to n - 1:   (left to right: "more than my left neighbour")
    if ratings[i] > ratings[i - 1]: candies[i] = candies[i - 1] + 1
for each i from n - 2 down to 0:   (right to left: "more than my right neighbour")
    if ratings[i] > ratings[i + 1]: candies[i] = max(candies[i], candies[i + 1] + 1)   (max keeps the first pass true)
return sum of candies

min_number_operations.optimal:
operations = target[0]   (every stroke covering index 0 starts there)
for each i from 1 to n - 1:
    if target[i] > target[i - 1]:
        operations = operations + target[i] - target[i - 1]   (new strokes begin at a rise; falls end for free)
return operations

patching_array.optimal:
reach = 0, patches = 0, i = 0   (every sum in 1..reach is buildable)
while reach < n:
    if i < size of nums and nums[i] <= reach + 1:
        reach = reach + nums[i]   (no hole: [1, reach] + x covers [1, reach + x])
        i = i + 1
    else:
        reach = reach + reach + 1   (patch with reach + 1: coverage doubles)
        patches = patches + 1
return patches

set_intersection_size_at_least_two.brute:
lowest = smallest start, highest = largest end
points = lowest..highest
for each size from 2 upward:
    for each subset of points of that size:
        if every interval contains at least 2 chosen points: return size
return -1

couples_holding_hands.optimal:
n = number of couples
parent = union-find over couples 0..n - 1, components = n
for each couch (i, i + 1):
    a = find(couple of row[i]), b = find(couple of row[i + 1])
    if a != b:   (two different couples share a couch: link them)
        parent[a] = b
        components = components - 1
return n - components   (a cycle of k couples needs k - 1 swaps)
